# These are captured artifacts: bytes read off a live service, pinned by
# digests the tests verify. Any line-ending conversion is corruption — a
# CRLF checkout rewrote the JSONL files on Windows and every byte-identity
# test failed on bytes git had changed, not bytes the code produced.
# -text disables conversion in BOTH directions (checkout and checkin),
# where eol=lf would still normalize on checkin; captured bytes must pass
# through untouched whatever they contain.
* -text
